Advantages:

Modern HTML and CSS: Chromium-based rendering supports CSS Grid, Flexbox, JavaScript, and web fonts, addressing limitations of wkhtmltopdf's older rendering engine.

Simpler browser dependency management: Developers do not need to maintain a separate ChromeDriver installation or manually launch Chrome for each PDF conversion.

Server-side PDF generation: Reports can be generated from HTML strings, local files, or URLs without requiring users to open a browser print dialog.

Start by parsing a JSON string using JsonNode.Parse().

Unlike JsonDocument, you don't need a using statement—JsonNode doesn't implement IDisposable.

```text
string jsonString = """
{
  "city": "Chennai",
  "temperature": 15,
  "conditions": ["cloudy", "windy"]
}
""";

JsonNode weatherNode = JsonNode.Parse(jsonString);

// Output the JSON as a formatted string
var options = new JsonSerializerOptions { WriteIndented = true };
Console.WriteLine(weatherNode.ToJsonString(options));
```

Access properties using indexer syntax.

You can chain property access for nested objects.

```text
