The final step is to register it in the Dependency Injection container and add it to the HttpClient pipeline as shown below.

```text
var builder = WebAssemblyHostBuilder.CreateDefault(args);

builder.Services.AddTransient<CustomHeaderMessageHandler>();

builder.Services
       .AddHttpClient<ILoveDotNetService>(client => client.BaseAddress = new Uri("https://ilovedotnet.org/"))
       .AddHttpMessageHandler<CustomHeaderMessageHandler>();
       //.AddHttpMessageHandler<AnotherCustomMessageHandler>();
```

That's it.

Now if you check the network tab in the browser, you will see the custom header added to all the requests sent to https://ilovedotnet.org.

