This interface has too many responsibilities.

If a consumer only needs to read data, it is still forced to depend on all the write and transaction methods.

This makes the code harder to maintain and violates the Interface Segregation Principle.

To follow ISP, you can split this large interface into smaller, more focused interfaces.

For example, you can create a IAsyncReadRepository<T> for read operations and let IAsyncRepository<T> inherit from it for write operations:

