When searching, some of the methods will actually throw an exception if you don't find anything based on the expression.

So, for example, first, you pass in your lambda expression of what you're looking for.

It searches backward in the collection and finds that last one that matches the expression and returns that.

If it doesn't find it, it throws an exception.

```text
